{"custom_id":"s-ap_calculus_ab-f09-k0","ok":true,"model":"claude-opus-5-5","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfyPvNp3jgpkfNuoZhxc4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"There are three perpendicular fences (two ends plus the divider), each x m long. The fence opposite the wall is 150/x m.\n\nC(x) = 6·3x + 12·(150/x) = 18x + 1800/x.\n\nC'(x) = 18 − 1800/x², which is 0 when x² = 100, so x = 10.\n\nC''(x) = 3600/x³ > 0 for every x > 0.\n\nC(10) = 180 + 180 = 360 dollars. The opposite fence is 150/10 = 15 m."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01D49qWHdJ6PbVwnvhK6JeMj","name":"submit_solution","input":{"answers":[{"item":"a","brief_reasoning":"There are three perpendicular fences (two ends and the divider), each x m, at $6/m. The fence opposite the wall is 150/x m at $12/m.","final_answer":"C(x) = 18x + 1800/x, for x > 0","ambiguous_or_flawed":false},{"item":"b","brief_reasoning":"C'(x) = 18 - 1800/x^2 = 0 gives x^2 = 100, so x = 10 (taking the positive root).","final_answer":"x = 10 m","ambiguous_or_flawed":false},{"item":"c","brief_reasoning":"C''(x) = 3600/x^3 > 0 for all x > 0, so C is concave up on its whole domain. x = 10 is the only critical point, so the relative minimum there is also the absolute minimum.","final_answer":"C''(x) = 3600/x^3 > 0 for all x > 0. C is concave up everywhere and has only one critical point, so x = 10 gives the absolute minimum.","ambiguous_or_flawed":false},{"item":"d","brief_reasoning":"C(10) = 180 + 180 = 360. The opposite side is 150/10 = 15 m.","final_answer":"Minimum cost is $360; the fence opposite the wall is 15 m long","ambiguous_or_flawed":false}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":605,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":681,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_to